- Change summary:
  - Replaced `TIMER__vRegisterIRQVectorHandler(...)` with `TIMER__enRegisterIRQVectorHandler(...)` returning `TIMER_nERROR` and propagating the selected SCB registration result.
  - Replaced `TIMER__vEnInterruptVector(...)` and `TIMER__vDisInterruptVector(...)` with `TIMER__enEnableInterruptVector(...)` and `TIMER__enDisableInterruptVector(...)`, both returning the delegated NVIC status as `TIMER_nERROR`.
  - Replaced `TIMER__vInit(void)` with `TIMER__enInit(void)` so the ordered TIMER0A..TIMER7B registration sequence now stops and propagates the first IRQ-registration failure.
  - Updated active and commented TIMER caller sites in the project variants to the new `TIMER__en...` names.
  - Replaced the remaining obsolete `SCB__vRegisterIRQVectorHandler(...)` project callers with `SCB__enRegisterIRQVectorHandler(...)` in the scheduler variants that still referenced the removed symbol.
- Post-implementation audit:
  - The TIMER application interrupt register/vector wrappers now match the enum-returning application-wrapper pattern already used by SYSCTL, SYSEXC, SYSTICK, and other modules that delegate into SCB or NVIC.
  - The higher-level TIMER init helper was included in the redesign because leaving it `void` would still hide IRQ-registration failures after the lower wrapper conversion.
  - The only remaining references to the old TIMER and SCB wrapper names should now be historical notes in progress logs rather than live code.